The  slave device provides to a process an interface identical to
that described in However, whereas all other devices  which  pro‐
vide  the  interface  described in have a hardware device of some
sort behind them, the slave device has, instead, another  process
manipulating  it  through the master half of the pseudo terminal.
That is, anything written on the master device is  given  to  the
slave device as input and anything written on the slave device is
presented  as  input on the master device.  Pseudo terminal pairs
are allocated on as‐needed basis, maximum number of them is  con‐
trolled  via sysctl (defaults to 992).  The following calls apply
